  "problem": "P05",
  "scope": "For one compact Chern--Ricci-flat strictly LCK metric, the integrated squared anti-J-invariant Lee derivative equals half the integrated squared Lee divergence. Gauduchon, zero Lee divergence, holomorphic Lee dual and Vaisman are equivalent for that metric. Ordinary Bott--Chern vanishing gives a unique flat conformal gauge up to scale. An explicit fixed Kodaira surface has a flat strict LCK gauge whose conformal class contains no flat Gauduchon representative, while the same complex surface has an explicit Vaisman metric. The arbitrary same-complex-manifold existence question remains unresolved.",
